# Prime Builder Implementation Report — WI-5638 Committed Terminal Archive Reconciliation

## Verdict

REVISED. The prior NO-ACTION (v005) was a stale auto-disposition. Implementation is now complete under the GO at v004.

## Implementation Summary

Added a fail-closed committed-terminal archive classifier (`classify_committed_archive_verdicts`) to `groundtruth_kb.bridge.versioned_files` and wired it into all live bridge queue readers:

1. **`versioned_files.py`** — New `classify_committed_archive_verdicts()` scans `archive/bridge-terminal-verdicts/` using bounded hidden-window Git probes. Trusts an archive disposition only when: tracked as a regular blob in HEAD, local raw bytes match the HEAD blob (SHA-256), first status is terminal, `Document:` slug matches, `Version:` matches, and the archive version is strictly newer than any live bridge version.

2. **`bridge_thread_files.py`** — New `index_bridge_thread_files_archive_aware()` wraps the existing `index_bridge_thread_files()` with archive suppression. Historical `versioned_bridge_files()` and `find_bridge_verdict_after()` remain unsuppressed for verdict reconciliation.

3. **`state_report.py`** — `_bridge_section()` now calls `index_bridge_thread_files_archive_aware()` instead of `index_bridge_thread_files()`, so `gt bridge state-report` excludes archived slugs.

4. **Tests** — 7 new tests in `platform_tests/scripts/test_archived_terminal_dispatch_reconciliation.py` covering: newer-archive suppression, equal-version non-suppression, dirty-file rejection, non-terminal rejection, Document mismatch rejection, untracked rejection, and state-report exclusion.

